WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.100
 Just because I'm
a girl, I should not

00:00:02.100 --> 00:00:05.010
be denied my right
to be in school.

00:00:05.010 --> 00:00:08.010
An advocate is someone
who sees an injustice

00:00:08.010 --> 00:00:11.760
and doesn't ignore it,
but wants to take action.

00:00:11.760 --> 00:00:15.090
I wanted to just go to
school without the worry

00:00:15.090 --> 00:00:17.880
that anyone would
kidnap me or stop me.

00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:18.900
That was my dream.

00:00:23.160 --> 00:00:28.060
On the 9th of October,
2012, the Taliban

00:00:28.060 --> 00:00:31.550
shot me on the left
side of my forehead.

00:00:31.550 --> 00:00:34.430
They shot my friends too.

00:00:34.430 --> 00:00:39.710
They thought that the
bullet would silence us,

00:00:39.710 --> 00:00:40.490
but they failed.

00:00:43.390 --> 00:00:46.000
I was receiving so much
support from around the world,

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:48.730
and I realized that I
could use it to speak out

00:00:48.730 --> 00:00:51.580
for girls everywhere who do
not have access to education

00:00:51.580 --> 00:00:52.120
right now.

00:00:54.840 --> 00:00:57.240
This class is for
anyone who wants

00:00:57.240 --> 00:01:01.220
to create a better,
fairer world for everyone.

00:01:01.220 --> 00:01:04.099
You will learn the
four-stage advocacy cycle.

00:01:04.099 --> 00:01:07.040
I will also be talking
to two amazing advocates,

00:01:07.040 --> 00:01:10.040
Amika George, who convinced
the UK government to provide

00:01:10.040 --> 00:01:12.050
free sanitary
products in school;

00:01:12.050 --> 00:01:15.680
and Lewis Iwu, who works with
leaders to develop strategies

00:01:15.680 --> 00:01:17.390
for their activism.

00:01:17.390 --> 00:01:19.430
Storytelling and
authenticity are

00:01:19.430 --> 00:01:23.510
very important as part of a
strong message for your cause.

00:01:23.510 --> 00:01:25.370
There are moments
when you get nervous,

00:01:25.370 --> 00:01:27.200
and you get a bit anxious.

00:01:27.200 --> 00:01:31.190
Those things are
common, they are normal.

00:01:31.190 --> 00:01:33.800
Hope and optimism are
the most important.

00:01:33.800 --> 00:01:35.847
That is what keeps you going.

00:01:35.847 --> 00:01:37.430
No matter where you
live in the world,

00:01:37.430 --> 00:01:39.770
how old you are,
where you come from,

00:01:39.770 --> 00:01:42.170
you can become a change maker.

00:01:42.170 --> 00:01:46.670
You can become an activist
in your community.

00:01:46.670 --> 00:01:50.590
I am Malala, and
this is MasterClass.

